<title>FRANCE: SBF says two French brokers to merge.</title>
<headline>SBF says two French brokers to merge.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French stockmarkets association SBF said on Monday that SBS Valeurs (France) SA and SBC Warburg Securities (France) SAS would merge.</p>
<p>The new SBS-SBC entity will be known as SBC Warburg (France) Entreprise d'investissement and will operate from January 2 as a member of the SBF-Bourse de Paris and Monep.</p>
<p>SBC Warburg is part of Swiss Bank Corp.</p>
<p>The association also said that Banque Bruxelles Lambert France would absorb its subsidiary BBL Intermediation SA.</p>
<p>Banque Bruxelles Lambert France will be active from December 31 as a member of the SBF-Bourse de Paris and Monep.</p>
</text>
